From estuart-SZLOfyx5T3qHXe+LvDLADg at public.gmane.org  Sat Mar 23 18:53:26 2013
From: estuart-SZLOfyx5T3qHXe+LvDLADg at public.gmane.org (Stuart, Elizabeth A.)
Date: Sat, 23 Mar 2013 14:53:26 -0400
Subject: Re: Value distance shows NA in nearest neighborhood matching
In-Reply-To: <514DCA5E.1030309@gmail.com>
References: <514DCA5E.1030309@gmail.com>
Message-ID: <F1EDAA88-C04B-4E79-A6A4-1ADD59198BF3@jhsph.edu>

Hi Nayan,
I believe that that is because there isn't a single "distance" measure that makes sense.

With Mahalanobis matching the Mahalanobis distance is calculated between each treated subject and each control (so if there are 100 treated and 200 control there are 100*200 Mahalanobis distances potentially calculated).  So there isn't just a single number that could be put in a vector, one number for each person.

Liz

